        'Solutions and concentration — Class 11 (Sindh Board)', 'Assalam-o-Alaikum dear students, I have prepared these comprehensive notes on Solutions and Concentration to help you master this fundamental chapter for your Sindh Board examinations. Understanding how solutes interact with solvents is vital, especially when applying the molarity formula $M = n/V$ or calculating mass percentage using $w/w% = (mass of solute / mass of solution) \times 100$. Always remember that $n = mass/molar mass$ and the dilution principle is governed by $$M_1V_1 = M_2V_2$$. Focus on these concepts, as they form the bedrock of your practical chemistry and analytical calculations in the coming years.', 'Chemistry',
