        'commons_anon_topic_10', 'commons_anon_topic_10-complex-numbers-class-11-sindh-board', 'notes',
        'Complex numbers — Class 11 (Sindh Board)', 'Assalam-o-Alaikum students, I have prepared these revision notes to help you master the fundamental concepts of complex numbers for your upcoming Sindh Board examinations. Understanding the imaginary unit $i = \sqrt{-1}$ is essential for solving quadratic equations that lack real roots. You will find that any complex number can be expressed in the standard form $z = a + bi$, where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers. Remember that the modulus of a complex number is defined as $|z| = \sqrt{a^2 + b^2}$, and for any two complex numbers, the product of conjugates follows $z \bar{z} = |z|^2$. Keep practicing these problems diligently to excel in your math assessments.', 'Mathematics',
