        'Electromagnetism — Class 10 (Federal Board)', 'Assalam-o-Alaikum dear students, I have prepared these comprehensive notes on Electromagnetism to help you master the core concepts for your Federal Board exams. This topic is fundamental to physics, revolving around the relationship between electricity and magnetism as expressed by the force on a current-carrying conductor $F = I L B \sin(\theta)$ and the magnetic field around a solenoid $B = \mu_0 n I$. By understanding how moving charges create magnetic fields, you will easily grasp the working principles of motors and transformers that appear frequently in your papers.', 'Physics',
