        'commons_anon_topic_09', 'commons_anon_topic_09-introduction-to-differentiation-class-11-federal-board', 'notes',
        'Introduction to differentiation — Class 11 (Federal Board)', 'Assalam-o-Alaikum students, I have prepared these concise notes to help you master the fundamental concepts of differentiation for your Class 11 Mathematics exams. We begin by defining the derivative as the limit of the difference quotient, expressed as $f''(x) = \lim_{h \to 0} \frac{f(x+h) - f(x)}{h}$. You must also memorize the power rule, $\frac{d}{dx}(x^n) = nx^{n-1}$, and the product rule, $\frac{d}{dx}(uv) = u \frac{dv}{dx} + v \frac{du}{dx}$, to solve complex problems efficiently. Practice these derivations daily to build a strong foundation for your upcoming Federal Board assessments.', 'Mathematics',
