        'Chemical equilibrium — Class 11 (Sindh Board)', 'Assalam-o-Alaikum dear students, I have prepared these comprehensive notes on Chemical Equilibrium to help you master this fundamental chapter for your Sindh Board exams. Remember that equilibrium is reached when the rate of forward reaction equals the reverse, expressed as $Rate_f = Rate_r$, and the equilibrium constant is defined by the ratio $$K_c = [Products] / [Reactants]$$. Focus on understanding the dynamic nature of these systems, as it is a high-yield topic that frequently appears in both MCQs and long-form questions.', 'Chemistry',
