        'Current electricity — Class 10 (Sindh Board)', 'Assalam-o-Alaikum dear students, I have prepared these comprehensive notes on Current Electricity to help you master the fundamental concepts required for your Sindh Board examinations. This chapter is the backbone of your physics syllabus, centered around the relationship between potential difference and current, expressed as $$V = IR$$. By understanding how charges flow through conductors and how resistance affects this motion, you will easily handle problems involving energy dissipation, defined by $$P = I^2R$$. Let us work together to strengthen your grasp on these essential principles so you can approach your exams with complete confidence.', 'Physics',
