        'Waves and sound — Class 10 (Federal Board)', 'Assalam-o-Alaikum dear students, I have prepared these comprehensive notes on Waves and Sound to help you master this essential chapter for your Federal Board exams. Remember that understanding the relationship between speed, frequency, and wavelength, expressed as $v = f \lambda$, is the foundation of your success in this unit. As you study, keep in mind that the intensity level of sound is measured in decibels, often calculated using the logarithmic scale related to $$I = P / A$$. May these notes provide you with the clarity and confidence needed to excel in your upcoming Physics paper.', 'Physics',
