        'commons_anon_topic_07', 'commons_anon_topic_07-basic-trigonometric-ratios-class-10-federal-board', 'notes',
        'Basic trigonometric ratios — Class 10 (Federal Board)', 'Assalam-o-Alaikum dear students, I have prepared these concise notes to help you master the fundamental trigonometric ratios for your upcoming Federal Board exams. Remember that these ratios define the relationship between the angles and sides of a right-angled triangle, which are essential for solving complex problems. Always keep the mnemonic SOH CAH TOA in mind as you practice, utilizing the core definitions $\sin(\theta) = \frac{\text{Perpendicular}}{\text{Hypotenuse}}$, $\cos(\theta) = \frac{\text{Base}}{\text{Hypotenuse}}$, and $\tan(\theta) = \frac{\text{Perpendicular}}{\text{Base}}$. With consistent practice of these identities and the Pythagorean theorem $a^2 + b^2 = c^2$, you will surely excel in your mathematics assessment.', 'Mathematics',
