        'commons_anon_topic_44', 'commons_anon_topic_44-common-grammar-mistakes-class-10-sindh-board', 'notes',
        'Common grammar mistakes — Class 10 (Sindh Board)', 'Hello dear students. As we prepare for our upcoming English exams, let us refine our writing by avoiding common grammatical pitfalls. Precision is the key to high marks. Consider these essential tips for your papers. First, subject-verb agreement is vital. If your subject is singular, your verb must follow the rule $S_{singular} + V_{singular}$. Do not let intervening phrases confuse you. Second, avoid dangling modifiers. Ensure your descriptive phrases are placed directly next to the noun they modify to maintain clarity. Third, use parallel structure in lists. If you start with a noun, continue with nouns. Think of it as a balanced equation where $A + B = C$ holds true for your sentence components. Fourth, watch your tense consistency. Do not jump between past and present without a logical reason. Fifth, master your punctuation. A misplaced comma can change the entire meaning of a sentence, much like how a change in variables affects the outcome of $PV = nRT$. Remember that writing is a process of refinement, similar to calculating $F = ma$ where every variable must be accounted for correctly. Practice these rules daily to ensure your prose is polished and professional. You have the potential to excel if you remain attentive to these structural details. Good luck with your studies.', 'English',
        'Common grammar mistakes', 'Class 10 · Sindh Board', 'Class 10',
        'Sindh', 'text', '["english","grammar","revision","sindhboard","class10","writingtips","sindh","class-10"]',
