        'Heredity and genetics — Class 10 (Sindh Board)', 'Assalam-o-Alaikum dear students, I have prepared these comprehensive revision notes on Heredity and Genetics to help you master the core concepts for your upcoming Sindh Board examinations. Understanding how traits are passed down is fundamental, especially when we look at Mendel''s Law of Segregation, which states that alleles separate during gamete formation, often represented as a ratio of 3:1 in the F2 generation. Remember that the genotype determines the potential, while the phenotype is the observable expression, and mastering the Punnett square method is essential for solving problems involving $$P = G + E$$. Keep practicing these genetic crosses, as they are a high-yield topic in your exams, and always remember that $1/4$ probability applies to each individual offspring.', 'Biology',
