        'Electrochemistry — Class 10 (Sindh Board)', 'Assalam-o-Alaikum dear students, I have prepared these comprehensive notes on Electrochemistry to help you master the core concepts required for your Sindh Board examinations. Understanding the flow of electrons is vital, especially when we look at the relationship between chemical energy and electrical energy defined by $Delta G = -nFE$. Remember that in an electrolytic cell, the process is non-spontaneous and requires an external power source, whereas a galvanic cell generates electricity through a spontaneous reaction represented by the overall cell reaction $$Zn + Cu^{2+} -> Zn^{2+} + Cu$$. Keep these fundamental principles in mind as you prepare for your upcoming assessments.', 'Chemistry',
