        'Databases and SQL basics — Class 11 (Federal Board)', 'Assalam-o-Alaikum students, I have prepared these concise notes to help you master the fundamental concepts of databases and SQL for your upcoming Federal Board examinations. Understanding how we structure data is essential, especially when considering the relational model where $\text{Degree} = \text{Number of attributes}$ and $\text{Cardinality} = \text{Number of tuples}$. You should also focus on the basic syntax for data retrieval, such as $$\text{SELECT column FROM table WHERE condition}$$. These notes cover everything from normalization to complex queries, so please review them thoroughly to ensure you are well-prepared for the practical and theoretical sections of your paper.', 'Computer Science',
