        'commons_anon_topic_43', 'commons_anon_topic_43-active-and-passive-voice-class-9-federal-board', 'notes',
        'Active and passive voice — Class 9 (Federal Board)', 'Assalam-o-Alaikum dear students, I have prepared these comprehensive notes to help you master the transformation of sentences between active and passive voice for your upcoming Federal Board exams. Remember that in active voice, the subject performs the action, represented as $Subject + Verb + Object$, whereas in passive voice, the focus shifts to the object, often written as $Object + be + V3 + by + Subject$. By understanding these structural shifts, you will gain the confidence to express your thoughts with greater precision and clarity in your creative writing tasks. Let us practice these rules diligently to ensure you secure full marks in the grammar section of your paper.', 'English',
