        'commons_anon_topic_25', 'commons_anon_topic_25-acids-bases-and-salts-class-10-federal-board', 'notes',
        'Acids, bases and salts — Class 10 (Federal Board)', 'Assalam-o-Alaikum dear students, I have designed these revision notes to help you master the essential concepts of Acids, Bases, and Salts for your Federal Board exams. We will explore the various theories of acidity and learn how to calculate the strength of solutions using the pH scale where $pH = -log[H^+]$ and the ionic product of water is defined as $K_w = [H^+][OH^-] = 1.0 \times 10^{-14}$. By understanding the neutralization reaction $$Acid + Base \rightarrow Salt + Water$$, you will be well-prepared to solve both theoretical and numerical problems with confidence.', 'Chemistry',
