        'commons_anon_topic_15', 'commons_anon_topic_15-gravitation-class-9-federal-board', 'notes',
        'Gravitation — Class 9 (Federal Board)', 'Assalam-o-Alaikum dear students, I have compiled these essential notes on Gravitation to help you excel in your Federal Board examinations. Remember that every object in the universe attracts every other object with a force defined by Newton''s Law of Gravitation $F = G\frac{m_1 m_2}{r^2}$, while the acceleration due to gravity on the surface of Earth is given by $g = \frac{GM_e}{R_e^2}$. Always keep in mind that the weight of an object changes with altitude according to $g_h = g\frac{R_e^2}{(R_e+h)^2}$, and the fundamental relationship between mass and weight is $W = mg$. Stay focused on your derivations and practice these numerical formulas consistently to secure top marks.', 'Physics',
