        'Matrices and determinants — Class 10 (Federal Board)', 'Assalam-o-Alaikum students, today we explore the vital topic of Matrices and Determinants for Boardly Commons, which is a key part of your Class 10 Mathematics syllabus for the Federal Board. We will focus on finding the multiplicative inverse using the formula $A^{-1} = \frac{1}{|A|} \text{adj}(A)$ provided that the determinant $|A| \neq 0$. You must also become proficient in calculating the determinant of a $2 \times 2$ matrix using the rule $|A| = ad - bc$ to solve simultaneous linear equations. Mastering these operations along with the identity property $A \times I = I \times A = A$ will help you excel in both short and long questions.', 'Mathematics',
