        'commons_anon_topic_14', 'commons_anon_topic_14-work-energy-and-power-class-9-sindh-board', 'notes',
        'Work, energy and power — Class 9 (Sindh Board)', 'Assalam-o-Alaikum dear students, these revision notes for Boardly Commons are designed to clarify the essential principles of work, energy, and power as per your Sindh Board curriculum. Always remember that work done is $W = Fd \cos \theta$ and the kinetic energy of a body is $K.E. = \frac{1}{2}mv^2$. Furthermore, the potential energy stored in a body is defined by $P.E. = mgh$, and power is the rate at which work is performed, expressed as $P = \frac{W}{t}$. I encourage you to practice these derivations thoroughly to excel in your upcoming examinations.', 'Physics',
