        'Chemical bonding — Class 9 (Federal Board)', 'Assalam-o-Alaikum dear students, I have prepared these comprehensive notes on Chemical Bonding to help you master the fundamental forces that hold matter together. Understanding how atoms interact is crucial for your Federal Board exams, especially when dealing with the octet rule $ns^2 np^6$ and the formation of stable structures. Remember that the energy released during bond formation, represented by the change in enthalpy $\Delta H < 0$, is what makes compounds stable. Focus on these concepts to ensure you score full marks in your upcoming Chemistry paper.', 'Chemistry',
