        'Algebraic expressions and factorization — Class 9 (Federal Board)', 'Assalam-o-Alaikum dear students, I have prepared these comprehensive notes to help you master Algebraic Expressions and Factorization for your upcoming Federal Board exams. Understanding these concepts is essential, especially when dealing with identities like $$(a+b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2$$ and the difference of squares rule $a^2 - b^2 = (a-b)(a+b)$. Practice these diligently, as they form the foundation for all higher mathematics, including the quadratic formula $x = (-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}) / 2a$.', 'Mathematics',
