      ) VALUES (
        'commons_anon_topic_22', 'commons_anon_topic_22-periodic-table-trends-class-9-sindh-board', 'notes',
        'Periodic table trends — Class 9 (Sindh Board)', 'Hello students. As we prepare for our chemistry exams, mastering periodic trends is essential for understanding how elements behave. Remember that these patterns are dictated by the effective nuclear charge and the distance of valence electrons from the nucleus. Follow this checklist to ensure you are ready for your assessment. First, atomic radius generally decreases across a period because the increasing nuclear charge pulls electrons closer, which can be understood through the concept of effective nuclear charge $Z_{eff} = Z - S$. Second, ionization energy is the minimum energy required to remove an electron from the outermost shell of a gaseous atom, represented by the process $X(g) + 	ext{energy} ightarrow X^+(g) + e^-$. You will notice this value increases across a period as atoms hold their electrons more tightly due to higher attraction. Third, electronegativity measures the ability of an atom to attract a shared pair of electrons in a chemical bond. This trend increases as you move from left to right across the periodic table. Finally, remember that metallic character decreases as you move right. When comparing elements, always consider their position relative to the noble gases, which have a stable octet configuration denoted by the general valence shell electronic configuration $ns^2 np^6$. Keep practicing these concepts by sketching the trends on a blank periodic table. You have all the tools necessary to succeed in your chemistry paper. Stay focused and keep reviewing your notes daily.', 'Chemistry',
        'Periodic table trends', 'Class 9 · Sindh Board', 'Class 9',
        'Sindh', 'text', '["chemistry","periodic table","sindh board","class 9","science revision","atomic trends","sindh","class-9"]',
