        'commons_anon_topic_45', 'commons_anon_topic_45-number-systems-and-conversion-class-9-federal-board', 'notes',
        'Number systems and conversion — Class 9 (Federal Board)', 'Assalam-o-Alaikum dear students, I have prepared these comprehensive notes to help you master the fundamentals of number systems, which is a core pillar of your Class 9 Computer Science curriculum. Understanding how computers process data using binary logic is essential, especially when we look at the base-n representation defined by $N = d_n r^n + ... + d_1 r^1 + d_0 r^0$. By practicing these conversions, you will easily grasp how the decimal system relates to binary, octal, and hexadecimal bases, represented by the general form $$Base_{10} \rightarrow Base_{2, 8, 16}$$. Let us work through these concepts together to ensure you are fully prepared for your Federal Board exams.', 'Computer Science',
