        'Scalars and vectors — Class 9 (Federal Board)', 'Assalam-o-Alaikum dear students, I have compiled these essential notes to help you grasp the fundamental distinctions between scalars and vectors for your Federal Board examinations. Always remember that while scalars are defined by magnitude alone, vectors require both magnitude and direction, such as displacement $\vec{d}$ or velocity $\vec{v}$. To master vector resolution, keep in mind the trigonometric relations $F_x = F \cos \theta$ and $F_y = F \sin \theta$, which are crucial for solving your numerical problems. Finally, ensure you practice the head-to-tail rule to correctly determine the resultant vector $\vec{R} = \vec{A} + \vec{B}$ in your exams.', 'Physics',
